From 24eb4ac9a3c37283c4fd1716fd15cca1035a61c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jonaslacour <jonaslacour1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:30:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Metal] Do not re-advise the free pieces split off in
 alloc_at

metal_mmap_region keeps every free block MADV_FREE_REUSABLE: the
constructor advises the whole reserved range and free() advises each
freed range. alloc_at() nevertheless advised both pieces it split off a
free block as REUSABLE again. madvise costs time linear in the length of
the range, and the tail piece spans most of the region (10x physical RAM
of address space), so every shared or host USM allocation paid ~70 us
per call, several calls per allocation.

The pieces are already in that state; only the allocated range changes
state (MADV_FREE_REUSE, unchanged).

On an M5 Max: malloc_shared+free of 1 KiB, 74 us -> 6 us per pair. A
BatchLAS test making ~1.3M small shared allocations spent 88 of its first
100 s in madvise; it now runs to completion in 75 s with 2.3 s in madvise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/runtime/metal/metal_allocator.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/runtime/metal/metal_allocator.cpp b/src/runtime/metal/metal_allocator.cpp
index d96cd54c..66562eaf 100644
--- a/src/runtime/metal/metal_allocator.cpp
+++ b/src/runtime/metal/metal_allocator.cpp
@@ -133,12 +133,13 @@ struct metal_mmap_region {
     }
     size_t remaining = (ptr + it->second) - (static_cast<char*>(addr) + size);
     _free_blocks.erase(it);
+    // Every free block is already MADV_FREE_REUSABLE (constructor, free()), so
+    // the split-off pieces need no madvise. Re-advising them cost time linear in
+    // their size, and the tail piece spans most of the reserved region.
     if (remaining > 0) {
-      madvise(static_cast<char*>(addr) + size, remaining, MADV_FREE_REUSABLE);
       _free_blocks.emplace(static_cast<char*>(addr) + size, remaining);
     }
     if (ptr < static_cast<char*>(addr)) {
-      madvise(ptr, static_cast<char*>(addr) - ptr, MADV_FREE_REUSABLE);
       _free_blocks.emplace(ptr, static_cast<char*>(addr) - ptr);
     }
     madvise(addr, size, MADV_FREE_REUSE);
